MODULE: media/upload
FILES: src/app/api/upload/route.ts
RESPONSIBILITY: POST /api/upload — accepts multipart image uploads, validates type/size, saves to public/uploads/
KEY_FILES:
- src/app/api/upload/route.ts: upload endpoint, 68 lines, moderate (file validation + sanitization)
DEPENDENCIES:
- uses: next-auth: getServerSession for admin auth
- uses: fs/promises: writeFile, mkdir for file storage
- uses: crypto: randomBytes for unique filename generation
- imports: src/lib/auth: authOptions
INTERFACES:
- POST /api/upload: accepts FormData with "file" field, returns { url: string } with public path
ALLOWED_TYPES: image/jpeg, image/png, image/gif, image/webp
MAX_SIZE: 5MB (5 * 1024 * 1024)
FILENAME_PATTERN: ${timestamp}-${randomHex8}.${ext} (ext derived from MIME type, not user input)
TRAPS:
- [HIGH] Filename extension derived from MIME type map, not user-supplied filename | FIX: EXT_MAP object maps MIME to extension
- [LOW] path.basename double-check prevents directory traversal even if filename generation logic changes | FIX: sanitized !== filename check
DECISIONS:
- Use crypto.randomBytes(8) over Math.random() for filename uniqueness — cryptographic randomness prevents collisions under concurrent uploads
- Extension from MIME type not original filename — prevents extension spoofing attacks
CHANGELOG:
- F-010 | add: initial upload API with auth, validation, sanitization
